INT. DRAGON'S CAVERN - DENTAL CHAMBER - DAY

A vast cavern, hung with sacks of gold and a cracked mirror the size of a barn door. In the center, a throne-sized stone chair, strapped with iron. A huge reptilian jaw rests open on its headrest.

IGNATHRAX, a dragon the color of old copper, reclines with his lids half shut and a single enormous molar exposed. Beside him, MAGISTER ODALRIC PYM, 60s, in a leather apron and a headlamp, holds a pair of tongs the length of a broom. TAMSIN EKE, 20s, his apprentice, hovers at the foot of the chair with a bucket of cold well-water.

ODALRIC
Don't clench.

IGNATHRAX
I am not clenching.

ODALRIC
You are clenching with your entire jaw. Release the jaw.

IGNATHRAX
It is difficult to release a thing one has been clenching since the Third Age.

TAMSIN
Master, the molar's cracked at the root.

ODALRIC
I can see that, Tamsin.

TAMSIN
It's the left one. The one he ate the knight with.

IGNATHRAX
That is a lie. I chewed that knight carefully.

ODALRIC
Be that as it may, the crown has to come out.

IGNATHRAX
Will it hurt?

ODALRIC
Enormously.

IGNATHRAX
Then I will have a drink first.

ODALRIC
You may not have a drink. Your breath ignites.

IGNATHRAX
It is merely a mood.

TAMSIN
Master, he's sweating molten.

Odalric looks down. A slow rivulet of copper-colored sweat creeps along the stone floor, steaming. Tamsin pours the bucket over it. A hiss. A cloud of steam.

ODALRIC
Thank you, Tamsin.

IGNATHRAX
I did not ask for this. I merely wished to sleep on my gold.

ODALRIC
And you shall. After the tooth.

IGNATHRAX
Why must it be out?

ODALRIC
Because the infection will spread to the brain, and the brain will then burn the cavern down.

IGNATHRAX
(a long pause)
That is a fair argument.

ODALRIC
Open wide.

IGNATHRAX
Count to three.

ODALRIC
One.

He yanks. The tongs come away with a molar the size of a milk churn. Ignathrax roars; the cavern shakes; gold sacks tumble. Tamsin dives under the chair. Odalric holds the tooth aloft in triumph.

IGNATHRAX (CONT'D)
You said three!

ODALRIC
I lied.
